From db42caf51cbf3679e58448d7132142a4ddb8423a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: StachowiakDawid <dawidos234@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:38:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] gpiolib: shared: don't proxy the Exynos9820 USB/DP lane
 select GPIO

On arm64, GPIOs named by several DT nodes are handed out through
gpio-shared-proxy. The proxy needs the chip's get_direction(), which
the Samsung pinctrl GPIO chip does not implement, so every request
through it fails with -EOPNOTSUPP and the DisplayPort controller
failed to probe on its usb-dir GPIO. That pin is only read, by the
combo PHY and by DP (non-exclusive request). Skip
samsung,usbdp-port-gpios while scanning for shared GPIOs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpio/gpiolib-shared.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpio/gpiolib-shared.c b/drivers/gpio/gpiolib-shared.c
index edb04a5bb9..79f68dd9fa 100644
--- a/drivers/gpio/gpiolib-shared.c
+++ b/drivers/gpio/gpiolib-shared.c
@@ -188,6 +188,15 @@ static int gpio_shared_of_traverse(struct device_node *curr)
 		    strcmp(prop->name, "gpio") != 0)
 			continue;
 
+		/*
+		 * Exynos9820 USB/DP combo PHY: the lane select input is also read
+		 * by the DisplayPort controller, which requests it non-exclusively.
+		 * Both only read it; keep the direct (unproxied) access, the
+		 * Samsung GPIO chip has no get_direction() for the proxy.
+		 */
+		if (strcmp(prop->name, "samsung,usbdp-port-gpios") == 0)
+			continue;
+
 		count = of_count_phandle_with_args(curr, prop->name,
 						   "#gpio-cells");
 		if (count <= 0)
